wifi_management.pcap contains one IEEE 802.11 beacon frame copied with
tcpdump -c 1 from Network_Join_Nokia_Mobile.pcap, published by the
Wireshark project as a sample capture:

https://wiki.wireshark.org/uploads/__moin_import__/attachments/SampleCaptures/Network_Join_Nokia_Mobile.pcap

The upstream Wireshark source tree is GPL-2.0-or-later; this 164-byte
derivative is included under this project's GPL-2.0-or-later license.

wifi_management_pair.pcap contains the first two frames from the same source
and verifies that the global DLT_IEEE802_11 link type is retained for every
record in a multi-packet capture.

wifi_ipv4.pcap contains the first packet of http_PPI.cap, another Wireshark
sample capture. Its 84-byte PPI metadata header was removed; the original
IEEE 802.11 QoS data frame, LLC/SNAP header, IPv4 packet, timestamp, and
packet lengths are unchanged:

https://wiki.wireshark.org/uploads/e8cebabd278b76e3bc9edbd484c4d293/http_PPI.cap

wifi_ipv6.pcap combines the same public 802.11 QoS data header with the
project's ipv6_packet.pkt payload, using LLC/SNAP EtherType 0x86dd. It
exercises preservation of an IPv6 802.11 data frame without inventing an IP
packet.
